  "preamble": "Lowering and unrounding of [o] to the open back vowel [ɑ]. In Proto-Germanic, PIE short *o merged with *a, and the merged vowel is reconstructed as back /ɑ/ (PIE *gʰóstis > *gastiz /ˈɣɑs.tiz/ 'guest', *nókʷts > *nahts /ˈnɑxts/ 'night'). Gothic nahts continues the merged vowel. The long vowels *ō and *ā merged in the same way as /ɑː/, which was then rounded to /ɔː/.",
